# HAPI FHIR org.hl7.fhir.* 6.6.7 transitive CVEs
# -----------------------------------------------
# The org.hl7.fhir.* packages at version 6.6.7 are transitive dependencies of
# hapi-fhir-validation 8.6.6 and are tightly coupled to hapi-fhir core — attempting
# to upgrade them independently results in AbstractMethodError at runtime.
#
# The vulnerable packages we CAN upgrade (convertors, dstu2, dstu2016may, dstu3, r4b)
# are already overridden to 6.9.0 in pom.xml dependencyManagement.
# Remaining packages (model, support, utilities, r4, r5, validation) require a full
# hapi-fhir major version upgrade (to 9.x or a version that bundles 6.9.4+) to resolve.
#
# Exposure assessment (VEX):
# - CVE-2026-33180 (auth leak in redirects): not exposed — we do not use HAPI's
#   HTTP client redirect-following in any authenticated flow; all FHIR calls go
#   through our own Spring-managed HTTP stack.
# - CVE-2026-34359 (Authentication Credential Leakage via …): same rationale; no
#   FHIR server acting as HTTP client with credential-bearing outbound requests.
# - CVE-2026-34361 (FHIR Validator /loadIG SSRF): not exposed — we do not expose
#   HAPI's FHIR Validator HTTP service (/loadIG endpoint is not mounted).
# Risk: LOW. Tracked in issue (TODO: file issue) for the eventual HAPI 9.x upgrade.
CVE-2026-33180
CVE-2026-34359
CVE-2026-34361

# CVE-2026-45367 — HAPI FHIR org.hl7.fhir.r4 6.7.9: ReDoS via FHIRPath
# matches()/replaceMatches(). Fixed in 6.9.7, but org.hl7.fhir.r4 is in the group
# that CANNOT be upgraded independently of hapi-fhir core 8.8.1 (AbstractMethodError
# at runtime — same constraint as above; needs a HAPI major upgrade).
# Exposure assessment (VEX): the impact is CPU exhaustion (DoS), not data exposure.
# FHIRPath evaluation only runs inside authenticated CQL execution / FHIR validation,
# which is bounded by the execution thread pool + per-run timeout (PAT-066), so a
# crafted pattern degrades a single request rather than the service. Risk: LOW.
# Tracked for the HAPI 9.x upgrade alongside the entries above.
CVE-2026-45367

# CVE-2026-43869 — org.apache.thrift:libthrift 0.22.0: security bypass. No fixed
# version published upstream yet (Trivy reports "affected", no fix). VEX: libthrift
# is a transitive dependency; this application runs no Apache Thrift RPC server and
# exposes no Thrift endpoint (it is a Spring Boot REST + WebSocket service), so the
# bypass is not reachable. Risk: NEGLIGIBLE. Remove once an upstream fix ships.
CVE-2026-43869

# HAPI FHIR org.hl7.fhir.* — newly-surfaced CVEs (BUG-125)
# --------------------------------------------------------
# CVE-2026-55471 — org.hl7.fhir.utilities 6.7.9: XXE in XsltUtilities.saxonTransform.
# No fixed version for 6.7.9, and utilities is in the group that CANNOT be upgraded
# independently of hapi-fhir core 8.8.1 (AbstractMethodError — same constraint as above;
# needs a HAPI major upgrade).
# Exposure assessment (VEX): NOT reachable. This application performs no XSLT / StructureMap
# transformation — there is no call to XsltUtilities.saxonTransform / TransformerFactory /
# javax.xml.transform anywhere in the codebase (verified by source grep). The XXE sink is
# never invoked. Risk: NEGLIGIBLE.
CVE-2026-55471

# CVE-2026-55470 — org.hl7.fhir.convertors / org.hl7.fhir.validation: incomplete fix for
# CVE-2026-45367 (DSTU2 path). convertors is bumped to 6.9.10 in pom.xml (fix applied there);
# the residual is org.hl7.fhir.validation, coupled to hapi-fhir core with no independent fix.
# Exposure assessment (VEX): NOT exposed. The platform is R4-only and never performs DSTU2
# version conversion. CdsInvocationService explicitly detects a DSTU2 client server and falls
# back to the default R4 server (no DSTU2 resource is parsed/converted); "DSTU2" elsewhere is
# only a string label in CQL `using` declarations. Same family as the already-VEX'd
# CVE-2026-45367. Risk: LOW. Tracked for the HAPI 9.x upgrade.
CVE-2026-55470

# CVE-2026-49485 — org.hl7.fhir.core 6.9.7: ReDoS via FHIRPath matches()/replaceMatches()
# in the FHIR Validator HTTP endpoint. Fixed in 6.9.9 / 6.9.4.2. (BUG-130)
# The standalone model libs (dstu2/dstu2016may/dstu3/dstu3.support/r4b) ARE bumped to 6.9.9
# in pom.xml (fix applied there). The residual flagged modules are r4/r5/validation, which
# CANNOT be bumped past the hapi-fhir 8.8.1-bundled 6.9.7: javap shows 6.9.9's
# IValidationPolicyAdvisor adds abstract isSuppressMessageId(String,String,Object...) and
# relativeDatePlaceHolder() that 8.8.1's FhirDefaultPolicyAdvisor does not implement ->
# AbstractMethodError at runtime (same coupling constraint as CVE-2026-45367/55471 above).
# Exposure assessment (VEX): NOT exposed. The platform does not run or expose the FHIR
# Validator HTTP endpoint (validator.fhir.org-style service). FHIRPath regex evaluation in
# our validation paths comes from trusted IG profiles (TW Core, packaged at build time),
# not from user-supplied FHIRPath; user CQL executes on the cqframework engine, not
# fhir-core's FHIRPathEngine. Risk: LOW. Remove when a HAPI release bundles core >= 6.9.9.
CVE-2026-49485
